  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The heart of BC: deciding whether an infinite sum settles to a finite value, using a battery of convergence tests.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Watch the geometric series \\( \\sum_{n\\ge1}\\left(\\tfrac12\\right)^{n} \\) converge: each partial sum \\( S_N \\) climbs toward the limit \\( 1 \\) (the amber line).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Partial sums",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "bcSeriesCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "Partial sums of a geometric series approaching their limit",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "bcSeriesDataBtn",
          "panelId": "bcSeriesDataPanel",
          "descId": "bcSeriesDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "bcSeriesDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "Partial sums S(n) up to the current n",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "n",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "S(n)",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "bcSeriesN",
            "valueDisplayId": "bcSeriesNV",
            "label": {
              "en": "Terms <b>N =</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Terms N",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 1,
            "max": 12,
            "value": 4,
            "step": 1
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "bcSeriesSn",
            "label": {
              "en": "partial sum S_N",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "indigo",
            "value": "—"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "\\( S_N=1-\\left(\\tfrac12\\right)^{N}\\to1 \\); a geometric series converges because \\( |r|<1 \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Convergence tests",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<strong>nth-term test</strong>: if \\( a_n\\not\\to0 \\), the series diverges. A <strong>geometric</strong> series converges when \\( |r|<1 \\); a <strong>p-series</strong> when \\( p>1 \\). The <strong>comparison</strong>, <strong>ratio</strong>, and <strong>alternating series</strong> tests handle the rest.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Geometric",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\displaystyle\\sum ar^{n}=\\dfrac{a}{1-r} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "p-series",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "converges if \\( p>1 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Ratio test",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\lim\\left|\\dfrac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}\\right|<1 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Alternating",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "terms \\( \\downarrow 0 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example · Geometric sum",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Evaluate \\( \\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\left(\\tfrac12\\right)^{n} \\). \\[ \\frac{\\tfrac12}{1-\\tfrac12}=1. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Ratio test",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Determine whether \\(\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty\\dfrac{n!}{n^n}\\) converges.\\[L=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{(n+1)!/(n+1)^{n+1}}{n!/n^n}=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{n^n}{(n+1)^n}=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{n}{n+1}\\right)^n=\\frac{1}{e}<1.\\]<p>Ratio test: \\(L<1\\), so the series <strong>converges</strong>.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Find the interval of convergence of \\(\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty\\dfrac{(-1)^n x^n}{n}\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Ratio test: \\(|x|\\). Converges absolutely for \\(|x|<1\\). At \\(x=1\\): alternating harmonic series, converges. At \\(x=-1\\): harmonic series, diverges. Interval of convergence: \\(-1<x\\leq1\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
